Z||000019||87GTZ34||10-31-2001||11:27 AM||||Stimpy sorry to cut into your post but it looks like you're up an running...  <BR>Roger if you want some assistance I can help to troubleshoot your problems.  I just did one of these for a small bus. that moved up to cable modem and flushed out hidden issues.  A few patches from MS 'support' seems to have resolved the issues.  Here's a partial list of network errors in 98 but there are many, many more after all this is Microsoft were talking about. <A HREF="http://support.microsoft.com/support/windows/topics/win98/comm/commem.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://support.microsoft.com/support/windows/topics/win98/comm/commem.asp</A> <BR>Let me know||||reg||1
Z||000020||rogergarrison||10-31-2001||04:52 PM||||thanks, but waiting for my DSL box to come. Ill try that, if Im not satisfied with that, theyll take it back too. The Roadrunners already gone. my dial up averages 52,000bps||||reg||1
